{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"attribute","text":"@frozen"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"EntityQueryView"}],"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"mentions":["doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/QueryingAWorld"],"kind":"mentions"},{"content":[{"text":"Overview","type":"heading","anchor":"overview","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"You get a view from a world’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"query()"},{"type":"text","text":" method, which lists every live entity, and narrow it"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"with methods such as "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/EntityQueryView\/with(_:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/EntityQueryView\/without(_:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":". Use it when you need the entities"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"themselves, for example to despawn them or pass them to commands:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["var world = World()","world.spawn(Position(x: 0, y: 0), Frozen())","world.spawn(Position(x: 1, y: 1))","world.spawn(Frozen())","","for entity in world.query().with(Frozen.self, Position.self) {","    world.despawn(entity)","}","print(world.query().count)","\/\/ Prints \"2\""]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Like "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/QueryView"},{"type":"text","text":", a view is a snapshot of the world it came from, so the loop above can"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"change the world while it iterates."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"pat